; The level of a glide. A frame that glides its own filter go towards halfway to a neighbour's gn speaks more
; quietly than go, which its gain was made for. Per frame three cards in (gn, go, w, as glideb reads them); two
; out for the level's last step: mode 0 and 0 without a glide (w 10), else mode 4 and the factor c (in percent)
; that puts the power back. c is card 3 gn + 0, 1 or 2 (for w 3, 5 or 9) of record go of the glide table: it asks
; the host for the record (OUT at ask) and reads all 291 of its cards (INP at gc), keeping that one.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            frm     INP   gn       03-11: a frame; no glide, mode 0
  04                    INP   go
  05                    INP   w
  06                    CLA   w
  07                    SUB   ten
  08                    TAC   gl
  09                    OUT   z
  10                    OUT   z
  11                    JMP   frm
  12            gl      CLA   gn       12-27: p = 3 gn, + 1 for w 5, + 2 for w 9
  13                    ADD   gn
  14                    ADD   gn
  15                    STO   p
  16                    CLA   w
  17                    SUB   five
  18                    TAC   ask
  19                    CLA   p
  20                    ADD   00
  21                    STO   p
  22                    CLA   w
  23                    SUB   nine
  24                    TAC   ask
  25                    CLA   p
  26                    ADD   00
  27                    STO   p
  28            ask     OUT   go       28-45: record go, card p kept
  29                    CLA   n290
  30                    STO   i
  31            gc      INP   x
  32                    CLA   p
  33                    SUB   00
  34                    STO   p
  35                    TAC   chk
  36                    JMP   nx
  37            chk     ADD   00       (p was 0: this card)
  38                    TAC   nx
  39                    CLA   x
  40                    STO   c
  41            nx      CLA   i
  42                    SUB   00
  43                    STO   i
  44                    TAC   out
  45                    JMP   gc
  46            out     OUT   four     46-48: mode 4 and c
  47                    OUT   c
  48                    JMP   frm
  50            gn      DATA  0
  51            go      DATA  0
  52            w       DATA  0
  53            p       DATA  0
  54            i       DATA  0
  55            x       DATA  0
  56            c       DATA  0
  57            z       DATA  0
  58            ten     DATA  10
  59            five    DATA  5
  60            nine    DATA  9
  61            four    DATA  4
  62            n290    DATA  290
